<title>MALAYSIA: PACIFIC BANK ABORTS BUY INTO INSURER GREAT EASTERN.</title>
<headline>PACIFIC BANK ABORTS BUY INTO INSURER GREAT EASTERN.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kuala Lumpur-based Pacific Bank Bhd said on Saturday it has broken off talks with Singapore's Great Eastern Life Insurance Co Ltd (GEL) with a view of a taking up a stake in the company's Malaysian operations.</p>
<p>Despite this, both parties have expressed the desire to strengthen their working relationship in Malaysia, Pacific Bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;In practical terms, the activities and performance of Pacific Bank will not be adversely affected by the cessation of these discussions,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>In January, the bank called off a merger plan with Singapore's Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp Ltd.</p>
</text>
